[
{ type: install }
pqfreebsd is staged, not enforcing.

Intended operation is by a sufficiently advanced LLM that can follow
the skills in %%DATADIR%%/skills/SKILL.md. The port cannot measure
"advanced." Local GPU/CPU runtimes (make showconfig LOCALLLM):

    ollama       CPU / Vulkan; CUDA often via Linuxulator
    llama.cpp    llama-server (GGUF; CPU and GPU backends)
    LocalAI      OpenAI-compatible; wraps llama.cpp
    llamafile    single-file GGUF (runs on FreeBSD)
    vLLM         GPU serving; CUDA typically Linuxulator
    koboldcpp    llama.cpp server/GUI

Default OPTIONS: LLM OLLAMA LLAMACPP. Native local path is CPU and Vulkan.
CUDA on native FreeBSD is not assumed.

    pqfreebsd-llm-check
    sysrc pqfreebsd_llm_attested=YES
    service pqfreebsd teststage

via-port oneenforce is refused until attested. That is the install
conjunct, not A_M. A missing LLM does not un-prove high-integrity
overwrite protection on a box that was already labeled.

oneboot still requires BOOT_SATISFIED=YES. TPM is not this pass.
Do not kldload mac_lomac until a test window.

Sibling: freebsd-mac-grok (not vendored). Pin a commit.
{ type: remove }
Uninstall restores PREINSTALL *behavior* if you ran oneuninstall.
ZFS snapshots are not destroyed. pkg remove is not zfs rollback.
]
